# User-visible text goes through t() with flat, greppable keys

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: leaf (presentation).

## Use This When

- A view, container or notification shows text to a person.

## Stop Here If

- Every visible string is `t('<feature>.<component>.<element>')` with a static key present in the `en` catalog.

## Core rule

- Catalogs are flat JSON: `{ "user.profile.save": "Save" }`. No nested objects; the whole key is one string so a plain text search finds both the catalog entry and every use.
- Key shape: `<feature>.<component>.<element>[.<state>]`, kebab-case segments, the same namespace as `data-testid`.
- The argument of `t` is a literal. No concatenation, no template expressions, no variables; choose between two literal keys in code when the text depends on state.
- Parameters use `{name}` in the value; plurals use `.one` / `.other` keys selected by `Intl.PluralRules`.
- `en` is the base catalog and always complete. `es` may lag; `bun run i18n:check` lists the gap without failing, and fails on a key used in code but missing in `en`, on a dead `en` key, or on a non-literal key.
- Domain and application code returns codes, never text; presentation maps codes to keys.
